From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:47:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 139/151] Find: "In selection" for find, replace, replace all
 and the count

A new find bar option keeps Find next and previous, Replace, Replace
all, the match count and the match highlights inside a range: the
selection the option is turned on with. As in Notepad++, it turns on
by itself when the find bar opens with a selection over lines (or at
least 1024 bytes on one line). The range is drawn faintly behind the
matches, since Find next replaces the selection it came from.

The option is not saved in the config: it belongs to one selection.
Closing the find bar turns it off. Replace and Replace all move the
range's end by what they add and remove; any other edit (typing, undo)
turns the option off, as the range would no longer cover what was
selected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

